  "note": "Regenerated 2026-10-25 at git_sha 7c5038e (change rv32i-canonical-convergence-2026-10, C2).\n\nWHY (this is NOT a C2 performance change): the previous baseline was captured 2026-10-16 at\ngit_sha 37ab63f and no longer matches this machine, so `perf_regression` failed with ratios\n1.3x-6.9x on rows that C2 cannot possibly affect. Control experiment: `perf_tests --tc=07\n--tc=08` was run back-to-back on a pre-C2 worktree (5191c47) and on the C2 HEAD build, with\nIDENTICAL compile flags (-O3 -DNDEBUG -O2 -DNDEBUG -std=c++23) and identical source closure\n(the perf binaries do NOT include any include/cpu/ header, and src/** includes none either,\nso the cpphdl library is untouched by C2). Result: HEAD/pre-C2 ratio = 0.89-1.21 (mean ~1.03)\n=> C2 has NO measurable performance impact. Meanwhile pre-C2/baseline was 1.01-2.36x, i.e. the\nPRE-C2 build regressed by the same amount => the drift is ENVIRONMENTAL (shared 4-core host\nwith concurrent load from another project; cgroup has no CPU quota, no throttling observed).\nCorroborating row that C2 never touched: TC-08|regs=1000|interpreter measured\nbaseline 6591.8us / pre-C2 11043.4us / HEAD 10140.5us => HEAD/pre-C2 = 0.92.\n\nTC-09 ANCHORS (RESTORED, NOT DEGRADED): TC-09 could NOT be measured in this run (all 9 rows\nSKIPPED, skip_reason=\"no row for backend '...' params '...' in subprocess output\" -- the\n180s subprocess_runner.h timeout is insufficient for the ch_uint<32> arith chain, same root\ncause as the 2026-10-16 baseline). perf_regression.cpp does `if (base <= 0.0) continue;`, so a\nbaseline row that degrades to median_us=0 PERMANENTLY LEAVES the comparison set => letting\nTC-09 degrade would have silently dropped 6 anchors (TC-09 interpreter/jit x 3 depths) and\nmade any future real TC-09 regression INVISIBLE (verified: a synthetic 10x TC-09 regression\nis reported by the OLD baseline (6 regressions) but NOT by a TC-09-degraded baseline).\n=> The 6 TC-09 anchors are therefore RESTORED VERBATIM from the 2026-10-16 baseline (flagged\nwith the 'note_restored' field). They remain LIVE comparison anchors; only their recorded\nvalues are older (2026-10-16 machine state) => they run STRICT, not loose, if the machine\nslows down again -- the safe direction (false positives over silent misses).\n\nPREVIOUS baseline (2026-10-16, 37ab63f) values, kept for audit:\n  TC-07  depth=10    interpreter  median_us=     23383.1\n  TC-07  depth=10    jit          median_us=      2027.9\n  TC-07  depth=10    verilator    median_us=      1977.5\n  TC-07  depth=100   interpreter  median_us=    162996.5\n  TC-07  depth=100   jit          median_us=     12284.5\n  TC-07  depth=100   verilator    median_us=      1840.8\n  TC-07  depth=1000  interpreter  median_us=   1652993.8\n  TC-07  depth=1000  jit          median_us=    128344.4\n  TC-07  depth=1000  verilator    median_us=      1770.4\n  TC-08  regs=10     interpreter  median_us=      9056.9\n  TC-08  regs=10     jit          median_us=      2411.1\n  TC-08  regs=10     verilator    median_us=      2010.4\n  TC-08  regs=100    interpreter  median_us=      6463.6\n  TC-08  regs=100    jit          median_us=      2088.4\n  TC-08  regs=100    verilator    median_us=      1800.2\n  TC-08  regs=1000   interpreter  median_us=      6591.8\n  TC-08  regs=1000   jit          median_us=      2507.7\n  TC-08  regs=1000   verilator    median_us=      1753.5\n  TC-09  depth=10    interpreter  median_us=     82796.2\n  TC-09  depth=10    jit          median_us=      4873.1\n  TC-09  depth=100   interpreter  median_us=    786479.8\n  TC-09  depth=100   jit          median_us=     45310.8\n  TC-09  depth=1000  interpreter  median_us=   8489177.9\n  TC-09  depth=1000  jit          median_us=    484189.4\n  TC-11  regs=10     interpreter  median_us=     37458.6\n  TC-11  regs=10     jit          median_us=     37852.8\n  TC-11  regs=100    interpreter  median_us=    352604.4\n  TC-11  regs=100    jit          median_us=    341019.5\n  TC-11  regs=1000   interpreter  median_us=   3874533.2\n  TC-11  regs=1000   jit          median_us=   3556989.4\n\nQUANTIFIED LOOSENING DISCLOSURE (the gate's real-regression detection power was reduced):\nThe rows below are SLOWER than in the 2026-10-16 baseline, by more than their own\nper-backend threshold. They were captured on a NON-IDLE host, so the new baseline is\nLOOSER than the old one for these rows => a real regression on them must now be larger\nthan the old threshold to be reported:\n  TC-07  depth=100   jit          old=     12284.5  new=     23929.9  ratio=1.95x  (backend threshold 1.6x)\n\n  TC-07  depth=1000  jit          old=    128344.4  new=    232222.4  ratio=1.81x  (backend threshold 1.6x)\n\n  TC-07  depth=1000  verilator    old=      1770.4  new=      2302.5  ratio=1.30x  (backend threshold 1.3x)\n\n  TC-08  regs=100    jit          old=      2088.4  new=      4090.8  ratio=1.96x  (backend threshold 1.6x)\n\n  TC-08  regs=100    verilator    old=      1800.2  new=      2392.3  ratio=1.33x  (backend threshold 1.3x)\n\n  TC-08  regs=1000   jit          old=      2507.7  new=      5269.4  ratio=2.10x  (backend threshold 1.6x)\n\n  TC-08  regs=1000   verilator    old=      1753.5  new=      2338.1  ratio=1.33x  (backend threshold 1.3x)\n\n=> detection floor per backend (was -> now):\n  jit          : \u771f\u5b9e\u56de\u5f52\u9700 >= 2.10x \u624d\u62a5\u7ea2\uff08\u65e7 baseline \u4e0b\u53ea\u9700 1.6x\uff09\n  verilator    : \u771f\u5b9e\u56de\u5f52\u9700 >= 1.33x \u624d\u62a5\u7ea2\uff08\u65e7 baseline \u4e0b\u53ea\u9700 1.3x\uff09\n\nThis is NOT neutral: the gate is looser than before for these rows. scripts/verify_perf_baseline_anchors.sh\nnow enforces (a) row-set conservation, (b) anchor conservation (no PASS row may silently\ndegrade to median_us=0, which perf_regression would skip forever), and (c) that every row\nlooser than its threshold is named in this note. Re-baseline on an IDLE host to restore\nthe original detection power.\n\nNOTE for future maintainers:\n  1. This baseline was captured on a host that was NOT idle. If `perf_regression` fails again,\n     FIRST re-run the pre-C2-vs-HEAD control experiment. A genuine code regression shows up\n     as a STABLE ratio; environmental drift shows up as a VARIABLE ratio that also affects the\n     pre-C2 build and the interpreter rows.\n  2. When regenerating, ALWAYS check that no previously-PASS row silently drops to median_us=0\n     (perf_regression skips those) -- e.g. diff old vs new and look for '-status PASS' counts\n     going to zero, and restore those anchors the same way.\n\nTC-09 ANCHOR CAVEAT (read before fixing the subprocess timeout):\n  The 6 restored TC-09 anchors (interpreter/jit x depth=10/100/1000) record the\n  2026-10-16 machine state. This host is measurably SLOWER than that (see the\n  quantified loosening table above: 1.30x-2.10x on the rows that were re-measured\n  here). TC-09 is currently unmeasurable only because subprocess_runner.h's 180 s\n  timeout is too short for the ch_uint<32> arithmetic chain at depth=1000.\n  => As soon as somebody raises that timeout, these 6 rows WILL report a FALSE\n     regression on this host (the jit anchor is ~2x faster than this machine,\n     threshold 1.6x). 'Strict direction' is therefore NOT a hypothetical here:\n     it is a guaranteed false positive. => Whoever fixes the 180 s timeout MUST\n     re-capture TC-09 on the same machine in the same commit and let the\n     anchor-conservation guard's C3 (loosening disclosure) record the change.\n"
